# Quality gates for ccmux.
#
# The Go daemon's go.mod lives in daemon/, not at the root, so auto-detection finds
# no test command here. Without this file the repo can never record a green.
#
# This file REPLACES auto-detection. Anything not listed here stops being gated, so
# add a line when a stack is added rather than assuming detection will pick it up.
#
# Added 2026-08-29: gofmt, a Go complexity ratchet, and a syntax check for the
# web lens. Before them this file held only `go vet` + `go test`, so formatting
# reached /ship's AI review instead of a gate (61789a5 repaired gofmt in two api
# files). The other two are cheap floors under things nothing checked at all
# rather than fixes for a measured miss. All three are ordered before the Go
# gates because they fail in milliseconds.
#
# 2026-11-04: the native Mac app (Swift) was removed from main and kept on the
# `mac-app` branch, and its two guarded `swift build` / `swift test` lines went
# with it. They had only ever skipped on this Linux host.

# --- static checks first: they are the cheapest and fail fastest ---

# Formatting. See .claude/gates/gofmt.sh for why this is a script and not the
# one-liner it replaced: `gofmt -l` exits 2 with EMPTY stdout on a file that does
# not parse, so judging it by the emptiness of its output alone passed on
# unparseable Go.
bash .claude/gates/gofmt.sh

# Web lens syntax. daemon/web/ is four hand-written JS files with no build step,
# no bundler and no test harness, so until this line the only thing standing
# between a mistake in it and a release was review — which does catch things
# (1b06e8f, a stale row count fed to every lens, caught pre-v0.1.45) but is not
# a gate and does not run on every commit. `node --check` is only a parse — it
# catches typos and unbalanced braces, not logic — but that is the floor and it
# costs milliseconds. A lint pass with complexity/length caps is the obvious next
# step and deliberately NOT bundled here: it needs an eslint config and a
# node_modules this repo does not have, which is a bigger decision than a gate.
command -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "qa-gates: node not installed — cannot syntax-check daemon/web"; exit 1; }
for f in daemon/web/*.js; do node --check "$f" || exit 1; done

# The claude agent sidecar (daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/, Node ESM, embedded in
# the daemon). Added 2026-09-16 with the sidecar itself: parse every module, and run
# the tests of its SDK-free modules (the flag parser, the translator, the HTTP routes,
# the MCP mapper, the walls check, and the agent with the SDK injected) with node --test. They import no npm package,
# so no node_modules is needed here; serve.mjs, the entry point that imports the SDK
# and only wires the others together, is parse-checked only.
for f in daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/*.mjs; do node --check "$f" || exit 1; done
node --test daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/args.test.mjs daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/translate.test.mjs daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/routes.test.mjs daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/agent.test.mjs daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/mcp.test.mjs daemon/internal/agent/claudeserve/walls.test.mjs || exit 1

# Web lens smoke test. Added 2026-09-11 because the parse above is not enough:
# a const declared inside a function and referenced from module scope passes
# `node --check` and shipped a lens whose sidebar was empty on every load
# (fetchWorkspaces swallowed its own ReferenceError). This EVALUATES app.js in a
# stubbed browser and drives one path, so that class fails here instead of in a
# browser. See daemon/web/smoke_test.js for what it does and does not cover.
node daemon/web/smoke_test.js || exit 1

# Which ccmux window a browser window shows, and what a relaunch brings back
# (route.js), and which browser window a notification tap moves (sw.js, run
# in a vm against fake clients). Added 2026-11-02 with the rules themselves,
# and the same day which way a finger drag turns the wheel (touchscroll.js)
# and which swipes open and close the phone's session drawer (drawerswipe.js),
# and when an open page moves onto a newer lens build (update.js), and when a
# paste is an image that goes to the session's host (paste.js). 2026-11-03:
# how the task queue reads on screen (tasklist.js). 2026-11-04: what
# Shift+Enter sends in the browser terminal (keys.js), and how long a
# session row flashes (flash.js), and which sessions a reopened window
# wakes (windowwake.js). 2026-11-09: how long a dropped connection waits
# before it dials again (retry.js). 2026-11-10: how wide a drag leaves
# the left menu (sidebarresize.js), and what the cap across windows on
# the Settings page offers (tasksettings.js).
node --test daemon/web/route_test.js daemon/web/sw_test.js daemon/web/touchscroll_test.js daemon/web/drawerswipe_test.js daemon/web/update_test.js daemon/web/paste_test.js daemon/web/tasklist_test.js daemon/web/keys_test.js daemon/web/flash_test.js daemon/web/windowwake_test.js daemon/web/retry_test.js daemon/web/sidebarresize_test.js daemon/web/tasksettings_test.js || exit 1

# Go complexity, capped at 10, as a ratchet over frozen pre-existing debt.
# See .claude/gates/gocyclo.sh for why it is a ratchet and not a wall.
bash .claude/gates/gocyclo.sh

# --- then the real work ---
cd daemon && go vet ./...
cd daemon && go test ./...
